{"availability":"available","full":"IlyaNovikov-RD/rocket_classifier","name":"rocket_classifier","description":"Production-grade rocket trajectory classifier: 1.000000 OOB min-class-recall via LightGBM + Optuna + proximity salvo consensus. Physics-informed features, Streamlit demo, ONNX inference.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-26T14:40:21Z","updated":"2026-07-20T16:29:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://novikov-rocket-lab.streamlit.app/","topics":["classification","docker","feature-engineering","lightgbm","machine-learning","onnx","optuna","physics","pydantic","python","radar","shap","streamlit","trajectory-classification"],"demo":"https://novikov-rocket-lab.streamlit.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.497Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.497Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.497Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.497Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live Demo — novikov-rocket-lab.streamlit.app Adjust physics sliders and watch the LightGBM model classify trajectories in real time.","The problem is tabular classification on physics-engineered features with cross-trajectory context. LightGBM is the right choice for four structural reasons:","1. The feature set is inherently tabular, not sequential. The discriminative signal lives in aggregate statistics — muzzle velocity, apogee shape, salvo rank, launch position. These are scalar features per trajectory, not temporal sequences. Sequence models (CNN, Transformer) are designed to learn representations from raw time series; here the representations are already hand-crafted from physics. Asking a neural network to re-derive initialspeed from raw pings adds no information but introduces variance and training complexity."],"features":["Raw radar pings are aggregated into 32 scalar features per trajectory — 25 kinematic features from finite-difference physics (assumptions 1 & 2), plus 7 salvo and rebel-group features from DBSCAN clustering (assumption…","Why 32? Automated backward elimination on the full training set started from 83 candidates (76 kinematic + 7 salvo/group) and dropped 51 features that did not improve minclassrecall — they either encoded redundant…","Note on model inputs: At inference, 3 rebel-group class-prior columns are appended to the 32 selected features, giving the model 35 total inputs. These priors (global training class distribution: 68.6%/24.3%/7.1%) are…","Threshold biases: [0.000000, -0.253165, 1.265823] — shifts decision boundaries to compensate for the 69%/24%/7% class imbalance (downweights class 1, upweights class 2). Found via coarse→fine grid search on OOB…","classweight=\"balanced\" in LightGBM, which applies inverse-frequency weights (wi = N / (K Nj)) internally. Preferred over SMOTE because synthesizing trajectory feature vectors produces physically implausible combinations…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IlyaNovikov-RD/rocket_classifier/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9dc559df006d7e0cde669f46b6cfe4009990fb1ef0dc5d5de1a98d538cb24ddf","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.730Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.730Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Live Demo — novikov-rocket-lab.streamlit.app Adjust physics sliders and watch the LightGBM model classify trajectories in real time.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IlyaNovikov-RD/rocket_classifier/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9dc559df006d7e0cde669f46b6cfe4009990fb1ef0dc5d5de1a98d538cb24ddf","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IlyaNovikov-RD/rocket_classifier/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.731Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-20T16:29:45Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IlyaNovikov-RD/rocket_classifier/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:44.732Z","